.TH SDE-SETTINGS 1 "October 2026" "SDE 0.1 Alpha" "Selviana Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
sde-settings, sde-control-center \- the Control Center of the Selviana Desktop Environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-settings
[\-\-page \fIname\fR] [\-\-list\-pages] [\-\-choose\-avatar] [\-\-apply] [\-\-version]
.br
.B sde-control-center
[\fIthe same options\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBControl Center\fR gathers every setting of SDE on one overview, by category, with a search over all of them:
.TP
.B Personalization
Appearance (theme, accent color, interface size, text size, icon theme and the wallpaper grid of /usr/share/backgrounds, the desktop-base themes and ~/Pictures/Wallpapers), Desktop icons, Panel, Start Menu (size, recently added and most used applications), Action Center, Clock & Weather, Notifications, Effects and Lock Screen.
.TP
.B System
Display (\fBsde-display-settings\fR(1) when installed: arrangement, modes, scale and profiles), Sound (pactl), Power, Date & Time (time zone sync and network time), Users & Avatar, Default Applications, Startup Applications (\fBsde-system-monitor\fR(1)), Keyboard, Mouse & Touchpad.
.TP
.B Network & Internet
Network (nmcli), Proxy and Bluetooth (bluetoothctl).
.TP
.B Devices
Drives (gnome-disks, else the panel's Drives flyout) and Printers (system-config-printer, else the CUPS web interface).
.TP
.B Administration
Software Updater (\fBsde-update\fR(1)), Driver Manager, System Reports, System Monitor and the included applications.
.TP
.B About
The system, every graphics card (vendor and model from pci.ids or lspci, kernel driver, primary card) and the OpenGL renderer.
.PP
Tiles of separate programs show a small arrow; a program that is not installed falls back to the page of the Control Center, or says what to install. Changes apply immediately to running SDE programs.
.PP
\fBUsers & Avatar\fR shows the account picture, the real name (AccountsService \fBRealName\fR, changed with \fBSetRealName\fR), the user name and the account type (Administrator for members of the sudo group, else Standard). A stock picture of \fI/usr/share/Avatar\fR or a PNG, JPEG or SVG picture of your own (at most 10 MB) is cropped to its middle square, scaled to 256 x 256 pixels and written to \fI~/.face\fR (with the \fI~/.face.icon\fR link); AccountsService gets it for the login screen (\fBSetIconFile\fR). \fBRemove avatar\fR brings back the initials. The Start menu's account button offers the same pictures.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " name"
Open a page directly (also written \fB\-\-page=\fR\fIname\fR). Page names: home (overview), appearance, desktop, panel, start-menu, action-center, clock, notifications, effects, lock, display, sound, power, date-time, users, default-apps, input, touchpad, network, bluetooth, system, suite and about. The default is home.
.IP
Also accepted, for the panel's status flyouts and convenience: overview, control-center, wallpaper, wallpapers and background (Appearance, scrolled to the wallpapers), theme, icons (desktop), start, menu (start-menu), displays, screen, monitor, keyboard, mouse (input, scrolled to the mouse), audio, volume, media, microphone (sound), wifi, wi-fi, ethernet, vpn, internet, proxy (network, scrolled to the proxy), battery (power), updates (system), applications, apps (suite), quick (action-center), animations, compositor (effects), info and graphics (about), time, date, timezone (date-time), weather (clock), user, account, accounts, avatar, picture, face (users), screensaver (lock) and the default-apps names. An unknown name opens the overview with a warning.
.IP
Examples: \fBsde-settings \-\-page sound\fR, \fBsde-control-center \-\-page=users\fR, \fBsde-settings \-\-page wallpaper\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-pages
Print the page names, one per line, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-choose\-avatar
Open Users & Avatar and the file chooser for a picture of your own (the Start menu's \fBChoose a picture\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Apply the saved display, keyboard and pointer settings and exit (run by \fBsde-session\fR(1) at login).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/sde/sde.conf
System-wide default settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sde/sde.conf
Per-user settings, written by the Control Center.
.TP
.I ~/.face
The account picture (256 x 256 PNG); \fI~/.face.icon\fR links to it.
.TP
.I /usr/share/Avatar
The stock account pictures.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sde/session.log
Messages of the current session (the previous one is kept as \fIsession.log.old\fR).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SDE_AVATAR_DIR
Another folder of stock pictures (tests).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sde-session (1),
.BR sde-panel (1),
.BR sde-desktop (1),
.BR sde-notifyd (1),
.BR sde-display-settings (1),
.BR sde-lock (1)
